-- title:
--   Summing G over cosets of the idelic norm group
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ a finite Galois extension of $K$ whose degree $[L:K]$ is prime, and let $\sigma$ be a $K$-automorphism of $L$ such that every $K$-automorphism of $L$ lies in the subgroup of integral powers of $\sigma$ (so the Galois group is cyclic with generator $\sigma$). Fix a measurable-space structure on the idele group $(\mathbb{A}_K)^\times$ that is the Borel structure of its topology, and a Haar measure $\nu$ on it. Write $N$ for the idelic norm attached to the genuine adelic base change $\mathbb{A}_K \to \mathbb{A}_L$, that is, the map induced on units by the algebra norm of $\mathbb{A}_L$ over $\mathbb{A}_K$ taken with respect to the structure furnished by that base change (a ring homomorphism $\mathbb{A}_K \to \mathbb{A}_L$ extending $K \to L$, together with an $\mathbb{A}_K$-algebra isomorphism $\mathbb{A}_K \otimes_K L \cong \mathbb{A}_L$ carrying $1 \otimes l$ to $l$). Let $T \subseteq K^\times$ be such that every $a \in K^\times$ admits a unique $t$ with $t \in T$ and $a = t\,N_{L/K}(b)$ for some $b \in L^\times$, i.e. $T$ is a system of representatives for $K^\times / N_{L/K}(L^\times)$. Let $G : (\mathbb{A}_K)^\times \to \mathbb{C}$ be $\nu$-integrable with compact support. Then the set of $t \in T$ for which $\int_{\mathrm{range}\,N} G(\hat t\,u)\,d\nu(u) \neq 0$ is finite, where $\hat t$ denotes the principal idele of $t$, and the resulting finite sum over $t \in T$ of these integrals equals $\int_{S} G\,d\nu$, $S$ being the underlying set of the subgroup of $(\mathbb{A}_K)^\times$ generated by the principal ideles (the range of $K^\times \to (\mathbb{A}_K)^\times$) together with the range of $N$.
--
--   This is the coset decomposition of $K^\times\!\cdot N(\mathbb{A}_L^\times)$ into the translates of the open subgroup $N(\mathbb{A}_L^\times)$ by representatives of $K^\times$ modulo $N_{L/K}(L^\times)$, the disjointness of the translates resting on the Hasse norm theorem for cyclic extensions of prime degree. It is used in the comparison of elliptic terms, namely by [`AutomorphicForm.finsum_sigmaCentralizerDomain_ellipticNorm_eq_mul_sum_finsum_centralizerDomain_elliptic_of_forall_perClass`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.finsum_sigmaCentralizerDomain_ellipticNorm_eq_mul_sum_finsum_centralizerDomain_elliptic_of_forall_perClass).
